{{also|Derrick}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Derived from the name of British [[executioner]] {{w|Thomas Derrick}}, who invented the framework arrangement commonly known by this name to aid in the conduct of executions.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈdɛɹɪk/|lang=en}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛrɪk|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A device that is used for lifting and moving large objects.
# A [[framework]] that is constructed over a mine or oil well for the purpose of [[bore|boring]] or lowering pipes.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[hangman]].

===References===
* For "hangman": '''1949''', John Dover Wilson (compiler), '''Life in Shakespeare's England. A Book of Elizabethan Prose''', Cambridge at the University Press. 1st ed. 1911, 2nd ed. 1913, 8th reprint. In Glossary and Notes

